{"title":"where is my submarine?","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/where-is-my-submarine","date":1768885500000,"content":"<figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/d74d730d-492f-48cc-9762-66193e16f525/NC+winter+submarine.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"3803\" height=\"2852\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/d74d730d-492f-48cc-9762-66193e16f525/NC+winter+submarine.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/d74d730d-492f-48cc-9762-66193e16f525/NC+winter+submarine.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/d74d730d-492f-48cc-9762-66193e16f525/NC+winter+submarine.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/d74d730d-492f-48cc-9762-66193e16f525/NC+winter+submarine.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/d74d730d-492f-48cc-9762-66193e16f525/NC+winter+submarine.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/d74d730d-492f-48cc-9762-66193e16f525/NC+winter+submarine.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/d74d730d-492f-48cc-9762-66193e16f525/NC+winter+submarine.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <p><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/tag/sketchbook\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>life from my sketchbook</strong></a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p>after a few weeks of traveling — from my home in <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/drawing-through-a-life-rupture\" target=\"_blank\">Istanbul to Paris, then New York</a> — I arrived at my parents’ place in North Carolina on Christmas Day, and spent the next week walking in a dark and anxious haze. I wrote about those weeks — and the daily practices I leaned on — in a recent letter, <a href=\"https://buttondown.com/keningzhu/archive/daily-practices\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. one of my practices was walking for an hour through the forest trails behind my parents’ house. when I sat down at my sketchbook, that’s what I wanted to draw. </p><p>the sun was bright and blinding, but my perspective of it felt stark, and severe. I could sense into — and feel — the knife’s edge of my own being. </p><p>in this spread, I drew both the physical and emotional realities:  </p><ul><li><p><strong>what I saw</strong> — the bare winter trees (left page) </p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>what I felt</strong> — casting a dark spell, swimming to my submarine (right page) </p></li></ul>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5a8d4e0a-e088-45e0-9581-a4525ef40493/IMG_8321.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5a8d4e0a-e088-45e0-9581-a4525ef40493/IMG_8321.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5a8d4e0a-e088-45e0-9581-a4525ef40493/IMG_8321.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5a8d4e0a-e088-45e0-9581-a4525ef40493/IMG_8321.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5a8d4e0a-e088-45e0-9581-a4525ef40493/IMG_8321.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5a8d4e0a-e088-45e0-9581-a4525ef40493/IMG_8321.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5a8d4e0a-e088-45e0-9581-a4525ef40493/IMG_8321.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5a8d4e0a-e088-45e0-9581-a4525ef40493/IMG_8321.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <h1>why I make art</h1><p>I wrote on these pages: </p><p><em>“I wake up and feel something different everyday.” <br />”when I draw how I feel, somehow, I’m less afraid”</em></p><p>this is, in summary, why I make art. because making art is an act of witnessing — seeing, reflecting on, distilling — my own life experiences. it is a form of metabolism that makes life more bearable, more beautiful, less boring. it feels less like a tangle of meaningless randomness and more like a complex mystery that I’m a part of. I make art to feel sane, because the monsters and voices in my head (and in the world) are loud. deafening, sometimes. I make art to breathe better. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/71ab616b-f512-4db9-83a5-d379d55d9fce/NC+winter+submarine+3.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/71ab616b-f512-4db9-83a5-d379d55d9fce/NC+winter+submarine+3.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/71ab616b-f512-4db9-83a5-d379d55d9fce/NC+winter+submarine+3.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/71ab616b-f512-4db9-83a5-d379d55d9fce/NC+winter+submarine+3.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/71ab616b-f512-4db9-83a5-d379d55d9fce/NC+winter+submarine+3.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/71ab616b-f512-4db9-83a5-d379d55d9fce/NC+winter+submarine+3.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/71ab616b-f512-4db9-83a5-d379d55d9fce/NC+winter+submarine+3.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/71ab616b-f512-4db9-83a5-d379d55d9fce/NC+winter+submarine+3.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <h1><em>“was that the wrong spell?”</em> </h1><p>in the top image, I drew myself at the top of a cliff — as if ready to jump, as if in conversation with my dark magic, wielding a wand that felt like it belonged to me. but I felt a swirling chaotic dark force around me that told me <em>maybe you aren’t in control. maybe you can’t control what you’ve unleashed. maybe this will eat you alive. maybe you will regret this. </em></p><p>was that the wrong spell? for what? did I make the right choices? do I know what I’m doing? this applies on a day to day, micro-level, as well as the major life choices. sometimes I am so exhausted with making decisions that I don’t even know what to wear, or what to eat, or what to do with myself on any given day. </p><p>there is nothing like a violent change to make you question everything you once thought certain. I know that this period of swirly chaos is something I must live <em>through</em>. the chaos is a part of me. there is no right or wrong spell. there only <em>is this moment</em> — a series of moments that unfold, and my choice to trust in them, and in myself, or not. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/a3d1c10a-e223-4ec7-b9f0-a19e076c50d5/NC+winter+submarine+2.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/a3d1c10a-e223-4ec7-b9f0-a19e076c50d5/NC+winter+submarine+2.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/a3d1c10a-e223-4ec7-b9f0-a19e076c50d5/NC+winter+submarine+2.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/a3d1c10a-e223-4ec7-b9f0-a19e076c50d5/NC+winter+submarine+2.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/a3d1c10a-e223-4ec7-b9f0-a19e076c50d5/NC+winter+submarine+2.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/a3d1c10a-e223-4ec7-b9f0-a19e076c50d5/NC+winter+submarine+2.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/a3d1c10a-e223-4ec7-b9f0-a19e076c50d5/NC+winter+submarine+2.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/a3d1c10a-e223-4ec7-b9f0-a19e076c50d5/NC+winter+submarine+2.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <h1><em>where is my submarine?!?</em></h1><p>when I feel as though I’m drowning, I long for a submarine. I drew that feeling — swimming through the dark waters to a safe refuge: a windowless, black vessel where I could lay very, very still, be at the bottom of the ocean, and feel safe. </p><p>it was an impulse to cocoon myself during a difficult time. there’s a subtle psychological shift that happened when I realized that I was entering <strong><em>submarine time.</em></strong> in moving from the sensation of drowning; swimming in darkness — to finding the relief and comfort of a vessel. it is almost an act of giving myself permission to be <em>here</em>, at the bottom of the ocean. to make my home in this darkness. to find comfort in it. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/9bc32d1a-7aeb-4c48-a790-4605f9880b13/NC+winter+submarine+4.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/9bc32d1a-7aeb-4c48-a790-4605f9880b13/NC+winter+submarine+4.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/9bc32d1a-7aeb-4c48-a790-4605f9880b13/NC+winter+submarine+4.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/9bc32d1a-7aeb-4c48-a790-4605f9880b13/NC+winter+submarine+4.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/9bc32d1a-7aeb-4c48-a790-4605f9880b13/NC+winter+submarine+4.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/9bc32d1a-7aeb-4c48-a790-4605f9880b13/NC+winter+submarine+4.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/9bc32d1a-7aeb-4c48-a790-4605f9880b13/NC+winter+submarine+4.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/9bc32d1a-7aeb-4c48-a790-4605f9880b13/NC+winter+submarine+4.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <p>I drew this full spread in about 2 hours, at night, while listening to Rosalía’s new album, Lux, which is its own kind of incomprehensible chaos + legible pain. there is something satisfying about letting an entire album carry you through. </p><p>after I finished, I felt much, much better. lighter, as if having exorcized the dark anxiety. </p><p>drawing is such a metabolizing practice. I remind myself to do this, regularly. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p>more <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/tag/sketchbook\" target=\"_blank\">from my sketchbook</a><br />more <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/visual-art\" target=\"_blank\">visual art</a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n ","author":"Kening Zhu","siteTitle":"kening zhu","siteHash":"ef8a94b9fc20c32a4ee7d94ee971337d278e8b2fafe747123e4eb5cea026e84e","entryHash":"c603d2a31fc9ce34a10b6534ca21221253d106e227373afa6bd50a7152599961","category":"Sites"}